{
  "_what": "\u00a725 backlog 741's forbidden names, as one sha256 per name. THE NAMES ARE NOT HERE AND ARE NOT ANYWHERE IN THIS TREE. The guard hashes each candidate string out of this repo's own sources and asks whether the digest is below; a name can therefore be refused while appearing nowhere. Written only by tools/recut_forbidden.py.",
  "_sorted_by": "hex digest, NEVER by name. An alphabetical list would order these by the names it exists not to publish, handing a reader the first letter of every one and the neighbourhood of each.",
  "_rule": "a derived name is forbidden when it is compound snake_case -- 6 characters or more, carrying an underscore, with 2 or more non-empty segments. Measured at the landing: 52 of the manifest's 293 derived names pass, and the rule cuts collisions with this client's 70 source files from 45 to 7. `explicit` entries are OUTSIDE the rule and are forbidden whatever their shape.",
  "_derived_vs_explicit": "`derived` is reproducible from the staged artefacts and the allow side, and the gate re-derives it independently every run. `explicit` has NO live source -- the six names the regenerated manifest no longer carries, and the two the backlog row cites by hand -- so it is never re-derived, never removed, and is the half that stops the rework being a silent narrowing.",
  "_growth_and_departure": "growth re-cuts, departure refuses. A new name in a re-staged artefact is ordinary. A name that stops deriving is either a real drop or a broken derivation, and the two are indistinguishable from here, so --retire has to be asked for by a person.",
